  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 1. Expanding the rotated covector in the SoV basis\n- **Rotation.** Raising generators kill $e_8^T$ from the right and the Cartan only rescales it, so a lower-unipotent $n_-$ already gives the whole orbit up to scale. $\\rho$ here is ${\\rm adj}\\otimes\\det$, since $\\sum_aE_{aa}=3\\cdot\\mathbb 1$.\n- **Coefficients.** $c_\\mu$ is defined by $e_8^T\\rho(n_-)=\\sum_\\mu c_\\mu\\langle x_\\mu|$. It is computed as $c=d\\cdot G_{xy}^{-1}$, where $d_\\nu=e_8^T\\rho(n_-)|y_\\nu\\rangle$ and $G_{xy}=\\langle x_\\mu|y_\\nu\\rangle$ is triangular and $z$-independent. This is cheaper than inverting the symbolic $x$-matrix.\n- **Observation.** After `Simplify`, every $\\langle x_\\mu|$ is a constant covector, free of $z$ and $\\theta$, even though it was built from companion $t$'s. So the $c_\\mu$ are independent of the twist and of $\\theta$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* lower unipotent n_-; as a 3x3 matrix it is {{1,0,0},{k21,1,0},{k31,k32,1}} *)\ngL = MatrixExp[k21 Ee[2, 1]] . MatrixExp[k31 Ee[3, 1]] . MatrixExp[k32 Ee[3, 2]];\nrot = Expand[UnitVector[8, 8] . gL];\nchecks[\"raising E_ij (i<j) kill e8^T\"] = Union[Flatten[Table[UnitVector[8, 8] . Ee[i, j], {i, 3}, {j, i + 1, 3}]]] === {0};\nXmat = Simplify[Table[Flatten[xB[μ]], {μ, gtpats}]];\nchecks[\"<x_mu| free of z and θ\"] = FreeQ[Xmat, z | θ];\ndY = Table[Factor[(rot . yB[ν])[[1]]], {ν, gtpats}];\ncX = Factor[dY . Inverse[gramXY]];\nchecks[\"sum_mu c_mu <x_mu| = e8^T rho(n_-)\"] = Union[Flatten[Simplify[cX . Xmat - rot]]] === {0};\nGrid[Prepend[Transpose[{gtpats, Xmat, cX}], {\"μ\", \"<x_μ| (GT components)\", \"c_μ\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
