  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 4. When is the overlap a determinant of Q's?\n- **Known case.** The diagonal-frame formula of the clean notebook (Section 10) reads $\\Omega_{zw}P_{\\rm phys}|\\Psi_{B,z}\\rangle\\propto\\det N[Q^j_{B,z},Q_{i,{\\rm vac},w}]/\\Psi_Q^{B,z}(x_0)$. In the adjoint, $e_1^T$ and $e_8^T$ are Weyl images of each other, so $\\Omega_{zw}P_{\\rm phys}$ belongs to the rank-1 family of Section 3.\n- **Generalization.** Replace the bra's direct $Q$'s by arbitrary functions $F_i$. $\\det N$ only probes $F_i$ at $\\theta+mh$ with $m\\in\\{-2,-1,0,1\\}$, so it depends on 12 numbers $f_{i,m}$.\n- **The covector $\\varphi_F$.** It is defined by $\\varphi_F\\cdot\\Psi_B=\\det N[Q^j_B,F]/\\Psi_Q^B(x_0)$ on the 8 eigenkets of $t(G(z))$, normalized by $\\langle x_0|\\Psi\\rangle=1$. Since the eigenkets span the space, this fixes $\\varphi_F$ completely. The bra normalization $\\Phi_F(y_0)$ is dropped, because only $\\varphi_F$ up to scale matters.\n- **Questions.** Which $\\varphi_F$ are rank 1, and which rank-1 $X=ab^T$ are some $\\varphi_F$?\n\nThe state machinery below is verbatim from the clean notebook (numeric point $h=1/2$, $\\theta=2/7$, $z=(3/2,5/4,2/3)$, $w=(5/2,7/3,3/5)$, 60 digits).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ws = {w[1], w[2], w[3]};\npt = {h -> 1/2, θ -> 2/7, z[1] -> 3/2, z[2] -> 5/4, z[3] -> 2/3, w[1] -> 5/2, w[2] -> 7/3, w[3] -> 3/5};\nprec = 60; hN = h /. pt; thN = θ /. pt;\nmaxc[e_, var_] := Max[Abs[Flatten[CoefficientList[Chop[Expand[e], 10^-40], var]]], 0];\nwts = Union[Table[J0[k][p], {p, ps[{Λ}]}, {k, 3}]];\nnu[n_][xx_] := ν[n][xx] /. pt;\nopDir[tt_, Q_, xx_] := nu[1][xx] nu[1][xx + hN] nu[1][xx + 2 hN] Q[xx - hN] - (tt[[1]] /. u -> xx) nu[1][xx + hN] nu[1][xx + 2 hN] Q[xx] + (tt[[2]] /. u -> xx + hN) nu[1][xx + 2 hN] Q[xx + hN] - (tt[[3]] /. u -> xx + 2 hN) Q[xx + 2 hN];\nopDual[tt_, Q_, xx_] := nu[3][xx] nu[3][xx - hN] nu[3][xx - 2 hN] Q[xx + hN] - (tt[[1]] /. u -> xx) nu[3][xx - hN] nu[3][xx - 2 hN] Q[xx] + (tt[[2]] /. u -> xx) nu[3][xx - 2 hN] Q[xx - hN] - (tt[[3]] /. u -> xx) Q[xx - 2 hN];\nsolveQ[op_, tt_, zz_, s_] := Module[{c, eqs, ns, res = {}},\n  Do[If[res === {},\n    eqs = CoefficientList[Chop[Expand[op[tt, Function[yy, zz^(s (yy - X)/hN) Sum[c[j] yy^j, {j, 0, d}]], X]], 10^-40], X];\n    ns = If[eqs === {}, {UnitVector[d + 1, d + 1]}, NullSpace[N[Table[Coefficient[e, c[j]], {e, eqs}, {j, 0, d}], prec], Tolerance -> 10^-30]];\n    If[Length[ns] > 0, res = Expand[#/Coefficient[#, X, d]] &[Sum[ns[[1, j + 1]] X^j, {j, 0, d}]]]], {d, 0, 4}]; res];\nstateData[tw_] := Module[{twv = tw /. pt, tGn, mix, evR, vecR, evL, vecL, vals},\n  tGn = Table[Expand[tGt[tw, a, u] /. pt], {a, 3}];\n  mix = N[(tGn[[1]] + Pi tGn[[2]]) /. u -> 3/7, prec];\n  {evR, vecR} = Eigensystem[mix]; {evL, vecL} = Eigensystem[Transpose[mix]];\n  vals = Table[With[{k = Ordering[Abs[ψ], -1][[1]]}, Table[Chop[Expand[(N[tGn[[a]], prec] . ψ)[[k]]/ψ[[k]]], 10^-40], {a, 3}]], {ψ, vecR}];\n  <|\"tw\" -> twv, \"tGn\" -> tGn, \"vecR\" -> vecR, \"vecL\" -> Table[vecL[[First[Ordering[Abs[evL - evR[[A]]], 1]]]], {A, Length[evR]}], \"vals\" -> vals,\n    \"mu\" -> Table[First[MinimalBy[wts, Abs[(tt[[1]] /. u -> thN) - hN twv . #] &]], {tt, vals}],\n    \"qd\" -> Table[solveQ[opDir, tt, twv[[i]], -1], {tt, vals}, {i, 3}], \"qu\" -> Table[solveQ[opDual, tt, twv[[j]], 1], {tt, vals}, {j, 3}]|>];\nQD[S_, A_, i_, xx_] := N[S[\"tw\"][[i]]^(-xx/hN), prec] (S[\"qd\"][[A, i]] /. X -> xx);\nQU[S_, A_, j_, xx_] := N[S[\"tw\"][[j]]^(xx/hN), prec] (S[\"qu\"][[A, j]] /. X -> xx);\nSZ = stateData[zs]; SW = stateData[ws]; nS = Length[SZ[\"vals\"]];\nx0N = N[Flatten[xB[x0pat] /. pt], prec]; y0N = N[Flatten[yB[x0pat] /. pt], prec];\nketZ = Table[v/(x0N . v), {v, SZ[\"vecR\"]}];\nbraW = Table[wv/(wv . y0N), {wv, SW[\"vecL\"]}];\npolesN = Range[Λ[[3]], Λ[[1]]];\nwgt[n_] := 1/Product[(m - n) hN, {m, DeleteCases[polesN, n]}];\npsiQ[S_, B_] := (QU[S, B, 2, thN - 2 hN] QU[S, B, 3, thN - 3 hN] - QU[S, B, 3, thN - 2 hN] QU[S, B, 2, thN - 3 hN]) QU[S, B, 3, thN - hN];\nchecks[\"all Q's found\"] = FreeQ[{SZ[\"qd\"], SZ[\"qu\"], SW[\"qd\"], SW[\"qu\"]}, {}];\n{checks[\"all Q's found\"], SZ[\"mu\"], SW[\"mu\"]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
