  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* constructive: solve φ_F = φ_target for F (gauge: F1(θ-2h)=1, F2(θ-2h)=0, F3 irrelevant) *)\nfUnk = {f[1, -2] -> 1, f[1, -1] -> p1, f[1, 0] -> p2, f[1, 1] -> p3, f[2, -2] -> 0, f[2, -1] -> tt, f[2, 0] -> q2, f[2, 1] -> q3, f[3, -2] -> 0, f[3, -1] -> 0, f[3, 0] -> 0, f[3, 1] -> 0};\nφU = Expand[φFsym /. fUnk];\nfitRes[target_, nTry_] := Module[{eqs, res = {}, sol, tn = target/Norm[target]},\n   eqs = φU - tn;\n   Do[sol = Quiet[Check[FindRoot[eqs[[1 ;; 6]], Transpose[{{p1, p2, p3, q2, q3, tt}, RandomComplex[{-2 - 2 I, 2 + 2 I}, 6, WorkingPrecision -> 50]}], WorkingPrecision -> 45, MaxIterations -> 300], $Failed]];\n    If[sol =!= $Failed, AppendTo[res, Max[Abs[eqs /. sol]]]], {nTry}]; Min[res]];\nSeedRandom[67];\nchecks[\"fit: w eigen-bra (in image)\"] = fitRes[braW[[1]], 10];\nchecks[\"fit: (I) point (in image)\"] = fitRes[momOrb, 10];\nchecks[\"fit: (II) point (in image)\"] = fitRes[z1Orb, 10];\nchecks[\"fit: generic orbit point (NOT in image; best residual)\"] = fitRes[randOrb, 10];\nKeyTake[checks, {\"fit: w eigen-bra (in image)\", \"fit: (I) point (in image)\", \"fit: (II) point (in image)\", \"fit: generic orbit point (NOT in image; best residual)\"}]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {
    "toolId": "X23sZmlsZQ"
   }
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 4c. What the two components are\n**(I) = extremal eigen-bras of companion transfer matrices.**\n- Under the intertwiner, $\\varphi\\cdot\\sum_{ij}G_{ji}(E_{ij}-\\delta_{ij})\\mapsto[X,G^T]$. For $X=ab^T$ this is $a(Gb)^T-(G^Ta)b^T$. So $\\varphi_{ab}$ is an eigen-bra of $t(G)$ iff $Gb\\propto b$ and $G^Ta\\propto a$.\n- For a companion $G$ with eigenvalues $(\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma)$, the right eigenvectors are $(\\beta^2,\\beta,1)$. The left eigenvector for $\\alpha$ is $\\propto(1,-(\\beta+\\gamma),\\beta\\gamma)$, which depends only on the other two eigenvalues.\n- Hence: **$\\varphi_{ab}$ is a companion eigen-bra $\\iff b\\propto(\\beta^2,\\beta,1)$.** Then $a\\perp b$ fixes $\\gamma$ through $a_1x^2+a_2x+a_3=(x-\\beta)(x-\\gamma)$, and **the third twist eigenvalue $\\alpha$ is free**.\n- By the mixed-twist formula, $\\varphi_{ab}\\cdot\\Psi_{B,z}=\\det N[Q^j_{B,z},Q_{i,A,w}]/\\dots$ with $w=(\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma)$ for any $\\alpha$.\n- **Caution.** $G(sw)\\neq sG(w)$, so rescaling $w$ is not trivial. The trivial direction is $\\alpha$.\n\n**(II) is degenerate.**\n- Its covectors annihilate the two $z$-eigenkets with $\\mu_3=0$, namely $(2,1,0)$ and $(1,2,0)$.\n- They are realized by a rigid $F$ that kills those two $\\det N$'s. This piece depends on $z$ and does not come from a twist.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "SeedRandom[91];\nβI = 7/10; bI = {βI^2, βI, 1}; aI = N[Cross[bI, RandomReal[{-1, 1}, 3, WorkingPrecision -> 60]], prec];\nγI = -aI[[2]]/aI[[1]] - βI;\nchecks[\"(I): a ∝ (1, -(β+γ), βγ)\"] = Abs[aI[[3]]/aI[[1]] - βI γI];\nφI = φAB[aI, bI]; φI = φI/(φI . y0N);\n(* the same covector is an eigen-bra of t(G(α,β,γ)) for different α, and det N with that twist's Q's reproduces it *)\ncheckAlpha[α_] := Module[{S = stateData[{α, βI, γI}], brs, A0, FA, v},\n   brs = Table[wv/(wv . y0N), {wv, S[\"vecL\"]}];\n   A0 = First[Ordering[Table[Norm[brs[[A]] - φI], {A, nS}], 1]];\n   FA = Function[{i, m}, QD[S, A0, i, thN + m hN]];\n   v = φF[FA]; {Norm[brs[[A0]] - φI], Norm[v/(v . y0N) - φI], S[\"mu\"][[A0]]}];\nalphaRes = Table[checkAlpha[α], {α, {13/10, -2/3, 5/2}}];\nchecks[\"(I): eigen-bra of t(G(α,β,γ)), any α\"] = Max[alphaRes[[All, 1]]];\nchecks[\"(I): det N with Q's of (α,β,γ) reproduces it, any α\"] = Max[alphaRes[[All, 2]]];\n(* (II): kills exactly the mu3 = 0 kets *)\nSeedRandom[44];\nkillII = Table[With[{φ = z1Orb}, Abs[Table[φ . ketZ[[B]], {B, nS}]]/Norm[φ]], {3}];\nidxK = Flatten[Position[SZ[\"mu\"], {2, 1, 0} | {1, 2, 0}]];\nchecks[\"(II): kills the mu=(2,1,0),(1,2,0) kets\"] = Max[killII[[All, idxK]]];\nchecks[\"(II): smallest other overlap (not a zero test)\"] = Min[killII[[All, Complement[Range[nS], idxK]]]];\n{alphaRes[[All, 3]], KeyTake[checks, {\"(I): a ∝ (1, -(β+γ), βγ)\", \"(I): eigen-bra of t(G(α,β,γ)), any α\", \"(I): det N with Q's of (α,β,γ) reproduces it, any α\", \"(II): kills the mu=(2,1,0),(1,2,0) kets\", \"(II): smallest other overlap (not a zero test)\"}]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
