  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result 6c (prefactor).**\n- $e_1=t_1(\\theta)/h$ exactly.\n- $e_2$ is a quadratic polynomial in transfer-matrix data: it lies in the span of $\\{1,e_1,e_1^2,\\text{coefficients of }t_2(u)\\}$, a 5-dimensional subspace.\n- $e_3=\\prod_iz_i^{\\mu_i}$, the eigenvalue of $\\rho(G^T)$, is not a single fused $T_\\lambda$ at $\\theta+kh$. It is still a polynomial in the $t$'s, since the 8 eigenvalues are distinct, but no natural closed insertion was found.\n\n**Conclusion of 6c.**\n- **What works.** Ket-side shift×polynomial insertions are transfer-matrix insertions. Combined with the twist torus, every rotation becomes a single $\\det N$ times the diagonal factor $\\prod_ip(z_i)^{\\mu_i}$.\n- **The catch.** The factor is natural for $e_1$, quadratic for $e_2$, and has no clean form for $e_3$. So a *natural* insertion covers the torus directions only to first order (the Lie algebra, $\\rho_{\\rm Lie}(G^T)\\propto t_1-{\\rm const}$), not the finite group element.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 8. SoV operators acting on $\\Omega_{z,w}$\nThe SoV basis is $\\langle x_\\mu|=e_1^T O_\\mu$, where the $O_\\mu$ are the eight products of fused $t(z)$'s at $\\theta-2h$ from Section 1, including $T_{20}T_{10}^{-1}$.\n- **The covectors.** Replace $e_1^T$ by $\\Omega=\\Omega_{zw}P_{\\rm phys}$, which is $\\propto$ the weight-$(2,1,0)$ eigen-bra of $t(G(w))$, and form $\\Phi(c)=\\Omega\\sum_\\mu c_\\mu O_\\mu$.\n- **Factorization.** Each $O_\\mu$ commutes with $t(z)$, so\n$$\\Phi(c)\\cdot\\Psi_B=\\Big(\\sum_\\mu c_\\mu\\,o_\\mu(B)\\Big)\\,\\Omega\\cdot\\Psi_B,\\qquad o_\\mu(B)=\\frac{\\langle x_\\mu|\\Psi_B\\rangle}{\\langle x_0|\\Psi_B\\rangle}.$$\n  The first factor is a sum of products of $T_\\lambda(\\theta-2h)$, i.e. of Q-determinants. The second is $\\det N[Q_B,Q_{\\rm vac,w}]/(\\dots)$.\n- **Questions.** Which $c$ give rotations? Is there a universal $c$, independent of $\\Omega$, for the torus rotations $\\Omega\\,\\rho(p(G^T))$?",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "tFn0 = Association[Table[ab -> N[tF[ab, θ - 2 h] /. pt, prec], {ab, {{1, 0}, {1, 1}, {2, 0}, {2, 1}}}]];\nT20i = tFn0[{2, 0}] . Inverse[tFn0[{1, 0}]];\nOmu = Association[{\n    {{2}, {2, 1}} -> IdentityMatrix[8], {{2}, {1, 1}} -> tFn0[{1, 0}], {{1}, {1, 1}} -> tFn0[{1, 1}],\n    {{2}, {2, 0}} -> T20i, {{2}, {1, 0}} -> tFn0[{2, 0}], {{2}, {0, 0}} -> T20i . tFn0[{2, 0}],\n    {{1}, {1, 0}} -> T20i . tFn0[{1, 1}], {{1}, {0, 0}} -> T20i . tFn0[{2, 1}]}];\nchecks[\"8: e1^T O_mu = <x_mu|\"] = Max[Table[Norm[UnitVector[8, 1] . Omu[μ] - N[Flatten[xB[μ] /. pt], prec]], {μ, gtpats}]];\niVac = First[Flatten[Position[SW[\"mu\"], {2, 1, 0}]]];\nΩc = braW[[iVac]];\nchecks[\"8: Ω is rank 1 (on the e8 orbit)\"] = SingularValueList[Xof[Ωc] /. h -> hN, 2, Tolerance -> 0][[2]];\nomu = Table[N[Flatten[xB[μ] /. pt], prec] . ketZ[[B]], {B, nS}, {μ, gtpats}];   (* o_mu(B), since <x0|Psi_B> = 1 *)\nchecks[\"8: <Ω O_mu|Psi_B> = o_mu(B) <Ω|Psi_B>\"] = Max[Table[Abs[(Ωc . Omu[gtpats[[m]]] . ketZ[[B]])/(omu[[B, m]] (Ωc . ketZ[[B]])) - 1], {B, nS}, {m, 8}]];\n(* {Ω O_mu} spans all covectors, since o_mu(B) is invertible and Ω.Psi_B != 0 *)\nΩbasis = Table[Ωc . Omu[μ], {μ, gtpats}];\nchecks[\"8: rank of {Ω O_mu}\"] = MatrixRank[Ωbasis, Tolerance -> 10^-30];\nchecks[\"8: smallest |Ω.Psi_B| (not a zero test)\"] = Min[Abs[Table[Ωc . ketZ[[B]], {B, nS}]]/Norm[Ωc]];\nKeyTake[checks, Select[Keys[checks], StringStartsQ[#, \"8:\"] &]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"485294\" data-output-id=\"118\" data-out-n=\"1626\" data-sub-idx=\"13\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"37\" data-sub-start=\"16\" data-sub-end=\"16\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[1626]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-line-broken=\"1\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:16.3923em;vertical-align:-7.9462em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"col-align-r\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:8.4462em;\"><span style=\"top:-11.1062em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.5em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-9.6062em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.5em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-8.0821em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.5em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-6.5821em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.5em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-5.0579em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.5em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.5579em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.5em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.0338em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.5em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-0.5338em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.5em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:1.6262em;\"><span class=\"pstru