d\">1</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8641em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">76</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">10: y2 = ∞: &lt;x0|M(w)M(y) rank 1, several w and y1</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.9954em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.6875em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">6.0111067214059527131259988113222037847304514254333677316</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.4713em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.6875em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8641em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">60</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">10: finite y2, y1 != z_k: min defect (nonzero)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:0.6887em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.6875em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.002216739119216439012650961070</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\" style=\"color:gray;\"><span class=\"mord\" style=\"color:gray;\">⋮</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"color:gray;border-right-width:0em;border-top-width:1.5em;bottom:0em;\"></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:2.8487em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.6875em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\" style=\"color:gray;\"><span class=\"mord\" style=\"color:gray;\">⋮</span><span class=\"mord rule\" style=\"color:gray;border-right-width:0em;border-top-width:1.5em;bottom:0em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">2390143017062611751238967175</span><span class=\"mclose\">∣</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:-0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mclose\">⟩</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:7.1962em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[1723]= \\begin{aligned}\n  &\\langle\\!\\lvert \\text{10: M(y1, $\\infty$) $\\propto$ $\\rho$((y1 - G(z)\\^{}T)\\^{}-1) (operator identity)} \\\\\n  &\\to 3.89488828401522701\\times 10^{-60} \\\\\n  &,\\text{10: y2 = $\\infty$: any rotation . M stays rank 1} \\\\\n  &\\to 1.03129628636678762772025189143145193657663468165667752935 \\\\\n  &\\times 10^{-76},\\text{10: y2 = $\\infty$: <x0|M(w)M(y) rank 1, several w and y1} \\\\\n  &\\to 6.0111067214059527131259988113222037847304514254333677316 \\\\\n  &\\times 10^{-60},\\text{10: finite y2, y1 != z\\_k: min defect (nonzero)} \\\\\n  &\\to 0.002216739119216439012650961070{\\color{gray}\\vdots} \\\\\n  &{\\color{gray}\\vdots}2390143017062611751238967175\\rvert\\!\\rangle\n\\end{aligned}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "c5ae892f-d107-46d9-9073-792bc9d0250b"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result 10.** Here $\\langle x_0|M(w)M(y)=\\Omega_wM(y)$, with $\\Omega_y=e_1^TP_{pp}(y)$ depending only on $(y_1,y_2)$. The rank-1 condition, all $2\\times2$ minors of $X$ vanishing, is polynomial in $s_i=1/y_i$, and it was solved completely. The solution set has three kinds of component:\n1. **$y_2=\\infty$, any $y_1$: non-degenerate.**\n   - $M(y_1,\\infty)\\propto\\rho\\big((y_1-G(z)^T)^{-1}\\big)$ exactly, the resolvent of the ket twist, which is a twist-torus element.\n   - So $\\langle x_0|M(w)M(y)\\propto\\Omega_w\\,\\rho\\big((y_1-G(z)^T)^{-1}\\big)$ is a global rotation of $x_0$ for every $w$ and every $y_1$.\n   - It is genuinely different from $\\Omega_w$. It is the one-parameter sub-family $p(x)=1/(y_1-x)$ of the Section 8 torus family.\n2. **$y_1=z_k$, any $y_2$: degenerate.**\n   - $\\Omega_y$ kills 6 of the 8 kets, and the two survivors with $\\mu_k=2$ give eigen-bras with a common $a=l_k$.\n   - So the product lies in a pencil of rotations fixed by $z$: the poles of the resolvent.\n   - This includes the trivial points $y=\\sigma(z)$.\n3. **Nothing else.** With $y_2$ finite and $y_1\\neq z_k$, the product is never rank 1. After the line factors are divided out, all pairs of minors were solved, and the only remaining root lies on $s_2=0$.\n\nIn short, multiplying two vacuum-building SoV sums gives a rotation only when one of them is a resolvent of the ket twist. That yields a one-parameter enlargement $\\Omega_w\\to\\Omega_w\\,\\rho((y_1-G^T)^{-1})$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 10b. Does $(w_1,w_2,y_1)$ reach generic raising exponentials?\nThe orbit of $x_0=e_1^T$ is projectively 3-dimensional: $x_0\\,\\rho(e^{aE_{12}}e^{bE_{13}}e^{cE_{23}})$, since the lowering generators only rescale $x_0$. $\\Omega_w$ supplies 2 parameters and the resolvent supplies 1.\n- **Coordinates.** Write $X(\\varphi)=a\\,b^T$, normalized by $b_1=1$ and $a_3=1$. The three coordinates are $(b_2,b_3,a_2)$, which for an upper unipotent $n$ are functions of $(n_{12},n_{13},n_{23})$.\n- **Tests.** The Jacobian rank of $(w_1,w_2,y_1)\\mapsto$ coordinates, and an explicit solve for random targets.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "coordsOf[φ_] := Module[{Xn = Xof[φ] /. h -> hN, i, j, a, b}, i = First[Ordering[Norm /@ Xn, -1]]; j = First[Ordering[Norm /@ Transpose[Xn], -1]];\n   b = Xn[[i]]/Xn[[i, 1]]; a = Xn[[All, j]]/Xn[[3, j]]; {b[[2]], b[[3]], a[[2]]}];\nnUp[{p_, q_, r_}] := MatrixExp[p N[Ee[1, 2], prec]] . MatrixExp[q N[Ee[1, 3], prec]] . MatrixExp[r N[Ee[2, 3], prec]];\ntargetOf[pqr_] := UnitVector[8, 1] . nUp[pqr];\n(* the x0-orbit really is parametrized by (b2, b3, a2): Jacobian of (p,q,r) -> coords has rank 3 *)\nfdJac[f_, x0_, d_ : 10^-20] := Transpose[Table[(f[x0 + d UnitVector[Length[x0], k]] - f[x0 - d UnitVector[Length[x0], k]])/(2 d), {k, Length[x0]}]];\nchecks[\"10b: (p,q,r) -> coords rank 3\"] = MatrixRank[fdJac[coordsOf[targetOf[#]] &, N[{3/7, -2/5, 5/9}, prec]], Tolerance -> 10^-15];\nΦf[{w1_, w2_, y1_}] := Ωv[{w1, w2, 1}] . Ms0[1/y1];\nchecks[\"10b: (w1,w2,y1) -> coords rank (3 = generic)\"] = MatrixRank[fdJac[coordsOf[Φf[#]] &, N[{5/2, 7/3, 3}, prec]], Tolerance -> 10^-15];\nchecks[\"10b: (w1,w2) only -> coords rank (2)\"] = MatrixRank[fdJac[coordsOf[Ωv[{#[[1]], #[[2]], 1}]] &, N[{5/2, 7/3}, prec]], Tolerance -> 10^-15];\n(* explicit solve for random raising exponentials; numeric-only wrappers so FindRoot never passes symbols *)\nClear[cΦ]; cΦ[W1_?NumericQ, W2_?NumericQ, Y1_?NumericQ] := cΦ[W1, W2, Y1] = coordsOf[Φf[{W1, W2, Y1}]];\ncΦk[k_, W1_?NumericQ, W2_?NumericQ, Y1_?NumericQ] := cΦ[W1, W2, Y1][[k]];\nSeedRandom[83];\nsolveFor[pqr_] := Module[{tc = coordsOf[targetOf[pqr]], best = {Infinity, {}}, sol, r},\n   Do[sol = Quiet[Check[FindRoot[Table[cΦk[k, W1, W2, Y1] == tc[[k]], {k, 3}], Transpose[{{W1, W2, Y1}, RandomComplex[{-3 - 3 I, 3 + 3 I}, 3, WorkingPrecision -> 50]}], WorkingPrecision -> 40, MaxIterations -> 200], $Failed]];\n    If[sol =!= $Failed, r = Norm[coordsOf[Φf[{W1, W2, Y1} /. sol]] - tc]/Norm[tc]; If[r < best[[1]], best = {r, {W1, W2, Y1} /. sol}]]; If[best[[1]] < 10^-30, Break[]], {12}]; best];\nsolved = Table[With[{pqr = RandomComplex[{-1 - I, 1 + I}, 3, WorkingPrecision -> 60]}, {pqr, solveFor[pqr]}], {3}];\nchecks[\"10b: random raising exponentials reached (max residual)\"] = Max[solved[[All, 2, 1]]];\nchecks[\"10b: reached covector ∝ target (projective distance)\"] = Max[Table[With[{u = Φf[s[[2, 2]]], v = targetOf[s[[1]]]}, Norm[Normalize[u] - (Conjugate[Normalize[v]] . Normalize[u]) Normalize[v]]], {s, solved}]];\n{N[solved[[All, 2, 2]], 6], KeyTake[checks, Select[Keys[checks], StringStartsQ[#, \"10b\"] &]]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
