  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 9. Summary of checks\n**Answer to \"when is a rotated $e_8^T$ a determinant of Q's?\"** Write $m(x)=(x^2,x,1)$, $a=g^{-1}e_1$, $b=e_3^Tg$, and let $\\beta,\\gamma$ be the roots of $a\\cdot m(x)=0$.\n\n**A single $\\det N$ works only on two kinds of piece.** This holds for the canonical rows and for every one of the 72 row choices that reproduce eigen-bras:\n- **(I) $b\\propto m(\\beta)$.**\n  - This piece is the extremal eigen-bras of a companion $t(G(\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma))$, with $\\alpha$ free, and $F$ is that twist's direct Q's.\n  - It does not depend on $z$, and $\\Omega_{zw}P_{\\rm phys}$ is one point of it.\n- **(II$_k$) $a\\perp m(z_k)$.**\n  - The twist $(\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma)$ read off from $a$ shares the eigenvalue $z_k$ with the ket twist.\n  - These covectors kill the two kets with $\\mu_k=0$.\n  - Which $k$ appears depends on the row choice; each $k$ occurs for 24 of the 72.\n- **Generic rotations** are not a single determinant for any row choice.\n\n**Two determinants always work (4d).** Any rotation is $s_1\\det N+s_2\\det N$ over the two eigen-bras $e_\\alpha-e_\\beta$ and $e_\\alpha-e_\\gamma$ of one companion twist $(\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma)$.\n\n**One determinant times a torus factor always works (6c).**\n- Every rotation is $\\varphi_I\\,\\rho(p(G(z)^T))$, with $p$ quadratic, so $\\langle e_8|\\rho(g)|\\Psi_B\\rangle\\propto\\prod_ip(z_i)^{\\mu_i}\\cdot\\det N[Q_B,Q_{w}]$.\n- The factor is the eigenvalue of an operator commuting with $t(z)$. It is therefore a ket-side transfer-matrix insertion.\n\n**SoV operators on $\\Omega_{z,w}$ (8).**\n- $\\rho(p(G^T))=\\sum_\\mu c_\\mu(p)\\,O_\\mu$ exactly, with the same $t$-products that build the SoV basis. $c$ is cubic in $p$ with rational coefficients, and equals the SoV coefficients of $e_1^T\\rho(p(G^T))$.\n- So $\\Omega\\sum c_\\mu O_\\mu$ has overlap $[\\sum c_\\mu o_\\mu(B)]\\cdot\\det N$, and it reaches the 3-dimensional torus family $\\Omega\\rho(p(G^T))$.\n- Neither non-torus rotations nor a change of $w$ is a structured insertion.\n\n**Symmetries do not help (6a).** The only symmetry of the SoV basis is the twist rescaling $\\mathrm{diag}(t,1,1/t)$, which preserves (I).\n\n**Pass criteria.**\n- Boolean checks must be True.\n- Residuals must be below $10^{-25}$.\n- Counts are expected values: 6, 8, 3, 72, 5.\n- Entries marked \"nonzero\", \"NOT\" or \"smallest\" must be clearly nonzero, of order $10^{-5}$ or larger. The \"$e_k\\in$ span\" rows with residuals of order $10^{-2}$ are expected negatives.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "Grid[Prepend[KeyValueMap[{#1, If[NumericQ[#2], ScientificForm[N[#2, 3], 3], #2]} &, checks], {\"check\", \"value\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
